<BaseLayout
  title={"Omakase at JIN — A Menu in Motion"}
  description={"Explore the omakase philosophy and seasonal progression at JIN."}
  ogDescription={"Explore the omakase philosophy and seasonal progression at JIN."}
  canonicalPath={"/omakase.html"}
  stylesheet={"/inner.css"}
  script={"/inner.js"}
  active={"omakase"}
>
<main id="main">
<section class="inner-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="inner-hero-media"><img src="/assets/omakase-hero.webp" alt="An omakase progression across the JIN counter" loading="eager" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" width="1600" height="1000"></div>
  <div class="inner-hero-scrim"></div>
  <div class="inner-hero-content"><p class="hero-meta">Omakase · A menu in motion</p><h1 id="page-title">Trust is the <em>first ingredient.</em></h1><p class="hero-copy">An evening shaped course by course, guided by season, temperature, texture, and the quiet confidence of the chef.</p><a class="hero-scroll" href="#story">Explore <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
  <p class="hero-page">Omakase</p>
</section>
<section class="section-space page-wrap" id="story"><div class="menu-sequence"><h2 class="display-heading reveal">A progression, <em>never a script.</em></h2><div class="intro-copy reveal reveal-delay"><p>Omakase means placing the evening in the chef’s hands. The experience at JIN moves through freshness, warmth, depth, and clarity, with every course arriving at precisely its moment.</p><p>The sequence below is illustrative; the final menu will follow the best ingredients available.</p></div></div>
<div class="menu-gallery progression-gallery">
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/scallop.webp" alt="Delicate Hokkaido scallop opening course" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>The opening</h3><p>A bright, delicate first course that resets the palate and establishes the season.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/sashimi.webp" alt="Seasonal sashimi served on dark ceramic" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>From the sea</h3><p>Sashimi and composed bites chosen for texture, temperature, and natural sweetness.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/nigiri.webp" alt="Nigiri formed and served at the counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>At the counter</h3><p>Nigiri formed one piece at a time, seasoned and served at the exact moment it is ready.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/chawanmushi.webp" alt="Warm chawanmushi in a handmade ceramic cup" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>The warm course</h3><p>A pause of gentle heat and deeper aroma before the final movement of the menu.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal"><figure><img src="/assets/black-sesame.webp" alt="Black sesame dessert with seasonal fruit" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>The finish</h3><p>A clean, restrained dessert that closes the evening without breaking its rhythm.</p></div></article>
  <article class="dish reveal reveal-delay"><figure><img src="/assets/gyokuro-tea.webp" alt="Gyokuro tea service on the lacquer counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"></figure><div class="dish-info"><h3>The pairing</h3><p>Sake and tea selected to echo the menu’s changes in weight, texture, and temperature.</p></div></article>
</div></section>
<section class="quote-band"><blockquote class="reveal">No two evenings need to feel <em>identical.</em></blockquote><p class="reveal reveal-delay">What stays constant is attention: to the ingredient, the room, and the guest.</p></section>
<section class="section-space page-wrap"><div class="split-story"><figure class="split-media reveal"><img src="/assets/otoro-brush.webp" alt="Otoro nigiri receiving its final seasoning" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"><figcaption>Finished in front of you</figcaption></figure><div class="split-copy reveal reveal-delay"><h2>Season as <em>a guide.</em></h2><p>The menu responds to what is at its best. Fatty tuna may arrive with a delicate brush of nikiri; silver fish may be sharpened with acidity; uni may appear warm, cool, or entirely unadorned.</p><h3>Every decision has a reason.</h3><p>Temperature, pressure, seasoning, and timing are adjusted piece by piece. That precision is what makes the experience feel effortless.</p><a class="text-link" href="menu.html">Explore menu <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
<figure class="full-image parallax-media"><img src="/assets/omakase-hero.webp" alt="Omakase courses arranged across a stone counter" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="900"><figcaption>An illustrative progression at JIN</figcaption></figure>
<section class="next-page"><h2>Ready for <em>your evening?</em></h2><a href="reservations.html">Make an enquiry →</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
